What lastRefT Is

SEQ 328 R3 (2026-10-09): before D1 is built, WHICH FIELD IS lastREF at the moment a bare accessor
is read, on both roads. lastRefOf("label") is a report verb (measure.twk): it prints
LASTREF <label> <tag of the field lastREF holds>, reads only, and as a command it does not
move lastREF. It sits in the exact slot a bare read would take, so it sees lastREF then.

W   inside a walk, after ++lrCur                       -- the member
O   outside: lrOut(lrSolo) -- the argument; lrOut() -- the action itself (runAction's fallback)
X   after a call in the SAME juxtaposed item: lrEcho(lrOther) then the slot
Y   before a call in the same item
Z   the next statement after X and Y
X and Y are where the roads could differ: runAction writes lastREF = the call's argument,
so whether the slot is read before or after lrEcho decides what it sees.
